course: dictionary
lesson: 13883
title: Knotted and knot
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Mia's shoelaces were knotted, so she could not run.» Knotted here means tied in a knot. You can check this by swapping in your meaning: "Mia's shoelaces were tied in a knot, so she could not run." It still makes sense.
explain: Knotted can also mean twisted and tangled together. «Tom's hair was knotted after the windy walk» means his hair was all tangled up, not neat. The clue is the wind, which makes hair messy.
explain: Knotted can describe a feeling too. «Her stomach knotted when the teacher called her name.» Her stomach did not really tie itself in a knot. It felt tight and hard, because she was worried. Words like this paint a picture of how someone feels.
fact: Knotted means tied in a knot, or having knots.
fact: Knotted also means twisted and tangled together, like hair after the wind.
fact: «Knotted» can mean tight and hard, as in «her stomach knotted» when someone is worried.
fact: Knot is also a verb. «Sam knotted the string» means he tied it in a knot.
fact: Knotted is the past form of knot: knot, knots, knotted, knotting.
exercise: «Mia's shoelaces were knotted, so she could not run.» What does knotted mean? | *Tied in a knot | Cut into small pieces | Very long and straight | Clean and shiny
exercise: «Her stomach knotted when the teacher called her name.» What does knotted show? | *She felt tight with worry | She was dancing | Her tummy was full of cake | She was very hungry
exercise: «The climbing rope was knotted every metre.» Find and copy one word that means tied in a knot. | *knotted | rope | climbing | metre
test: «Tom's hair was knotted after the windy walk.» What does knotted mean? | Painted bright blue | *Twisted and tangled together | Brushed smooth and neat
test: «Sam knotted the string around the box.» What did Sam do? | Sang a song | Cut the string | *Tied the string in a knot | Lost the string
exam: «Ella checked her knotted rope before she climbed, because a loose knot can be dangerous.» What does knotted mean here? | Long and thin | Very old and broken | *Tied in a knot | Wet from the rain
